panvk: write allow_merging_workgroups after, not before, pan_postprocess_nir

panvk_compile_shader records whether a compute shader may have its workgroups
merged into a single larger one (valhall_can_merge_workgroups), then uses that
answer to pick the divergence-analysis options for lowering. Both decisions
read variant->info.cs.allow_merging_workgroups immediately, before the shader
is handed to panvk_compile_nir(), which calls pan_postprocess_nir(). That
function starts with memset(info, 0, sizeof(*info)) and fills the whole
pan_shader_info back in from scratch, so the flag the driver just wrote is
gone by the time the hardware descriptor is built. The field ends up false for
every compute shader, and any consumer that reads it later (workgroup-size
selection) takes the conservative but wrong path.

Keep the decision in a local for the lowering and divergence options, and
assign it to the shader info only after panvk_compile_nir has finished.

Ported from upstream Mesa cf98950a ("panvk: fix allow_merging_workgroups
logic"), which is not in the pinned Mesa tree.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -1576,15 +1576,16 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
 
       nir_shader *nir = info->nir;
 
+      bool allow_merging_workgroups = false;
 #if PAN_ARCH >= 9
       nir_shader_gather_info(nir, nir_shader_get_entrypoint(nir));
-      variant->info.cs.allow_merging_workgroups =
+      allow_merging_workgroups =
          valhall_can_merge_workgroups(nir);
 
       /* With merged workgroups, we need to use different divergence analysis
        * options to take into account that threads from different workgroups
        * may be in the same subgroup */
-      if (variant->info.cs.allow_merging_workgroups) {
+      if (allow_merging_workgroups) {
          nir->options = pan_get_nir_shader_compiler_options(
             PAN_ARCH, MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE, true);
          /* Invalidate the old divergence analysis */
@@ -1595,7 +1596,7 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
 
       panvk_lower_nir(dev, nir, info->set_layout_count, info->set_layouts,
                       info->robustness, state, &shader->desc_info,
-                      variant->info.cs.allow_merging_workgroups);
+                      allow_merging_workgroups);
 
       variant->own_bin = true;
 
@@ -1606,6 +1607,7 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
          panvk_shader_destroy(&dev->vk, &shader->vk, pAllocator);
          return result;
       }
+      variant->info.cs.allow_merging_workgroups = allow_merging_workgroups;
       break;
    }
 
